    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0070",
      "reading_order": 80,
      "section": "Adjust Upper Rack",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 322.8008,
        "t": 503.80814000000004,
        "r": 428.2243303999998,
        "b": 493.75507772307697
      },
      "content": "Adjust Upper Rack",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0071",
      "reading_order": 81,
      "section": "Adjust Upper Rack",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 326.4122,
        "t": 476.96966000000003,
        "r": 556.8517621999999,
        "b": 461.64965907058826
      },
      "content": "You can raise or lower the upper rack to fit all items in either the upper or lower rack."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0072",
      "reading_order": 82,
      "section": "To raise or lower the rack:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 326.4122,
        "t": 457.5571238,
        "r": 426.01013059999946,
        "b": 450.5972719230769
      },
      "content": "To raise or lower the rack:",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0073",
      "reading_order": 83,
      "section": "To raise or lower the rack:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 326.4121999999999,
        "t": 446.49346,
        "r": 570.8845549999999,
        "b": 397.76016947058815
      },
      "content": "Empty the rack. Pull the rack out halfway and take notice of the position of the carriage wheel assembly and side rail on each side of the rack. Lift up on the front of the rack while pulling the rack out all the way. The rack will then be completely free of the side rails. Reverse this action to re-engage the rack's carriage wheels onto the rails in the higher or lower position desired."
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0074",
      "reading_order": 84,
      "severity": "note",
      "content": "NOTE: The upper rack must be level.",
      "section": "To raise or lower the rack:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 326.4122,
        "t": 393.67416000000003,
        "r": 351.0821287999999,
        "b": 386.71430812307693
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0076",
      "reading_order": 86,
      "section": "2 Dishwasher Care DISHWASHER CARE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 228.6734,
        "t": 336.846,
        "r": 398.3953739999999,
        "b": 316.08831856410256
      },
      "content": "2 Dishwasher Care DISHWASHER CARE",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0077",
      "reading_order": 87,
      "section": "2 Dishwasher Care DISHWASHER CARE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 323.4703,
        "t": 308.63495,
        "r": 431.4183174499996,
        "b": 284.9070929705882
      },
      "content": "If you have a drain air gap, check and clean it if the dishwasher isn't draining well."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0078",
      "reading_order": 88,
      "section": "2 Dishwasher Care DISHWASHER CARE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 323.4703,
        "t": 280.8051395,
        "r": 434.79747050000003,
        "b": 257.08417883333334
      },
      "content": "To Reduce Risk of Property Damage During Vacation or Extended Time Without Use:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0079",
      "reading_order": 89,
      "section": "2 Dishwasher Care DISHWASHER CARE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 323.4702424,
        "t": 251.17785000000003,
        "r": 439.7746144499995,
        "b": 210.7130994705883
      },
      "content": "■ When you will not be using the dishwasher during the summer months, turn off the water and power supply to the dishwasher."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0080",
      "reading_order": 90,
      "section": "2 Dishwasher Care DISHWASHER CARE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 323.4702424,
        "t": 204.80285000000003,
        "r": 567.0161379499989,
        "b": 172.7025009705883
      },
      "content": "■ Make sure the water supply lines are protected against freezing conditions. Ice formations in the supply lines can increase water pressure and cause damage to your dishwasher or home. Damage from freezing is not covered by the warranty."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0081",
      "reading_order": 91,
      "section": "2 Dishwasher Care DISHWASHER CARE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 323.4702424,
        "t": 166.79774999999995,
        "r": 555.2139429999991,
        "b": 143.06994697058826
      },
      "content": "■ When storing your dishwasher in the winter, avoid water damage by having your dishwasher winterized by authorized service personnel."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0010",
      "reading_order": 92,
